THE NAHOURI EDUCATION SYSTEM

A Global Framework for Standardized Education

I. PURPOSE

The Nahouri Education System (NES) is a proposed global educational framework designed to establish a common baseline for education across nations while preserving local cultures, languages, histories, and traditions.

Its central principle is:

“Standardize knowledge, not culture. Universalize opportunity, not identity. Teach the past, master the present, and mathematically prepare for the future.”

⸻

II. THE NAHOURI SCHOOLING STANDARD

The standard pathway consists of 18 years of formal education, from approximately age 3 through age 21.

Grade	Name	Approx. Age
N1	Foundation I	3–4
N2	Foundation II	4–5
N3	Foundation III	5–6
N4	Primary I	6–7
N5	Primary II	7–8
N6	Primary III	8–9
N7	Primary IV	9–10
N8	Primary V	10–11
N9	Primary VI	11–12
N10	Secondary I	12–13
N11	Secondary II	13–14
N12	Secondary III	14–15
N13	Secondary IV	15–16
N14	Secondary V	16–17
N15	Secondary VI	17–18
N16	University I	18–19
N17	University II	19–20
N18	University III	20–21

Standard Formula

3 years Foundation + 6 years Primary + 6 years Secondary + 3 years University = 18 years

The objective is to establish a common international educational clock so that a student’s educational level can be understood regardless of the country in which they were educated.

