XIII. THE NAHOURI INTERNATIONAL GRADE NUMBER

The N-Grade Number provides a universal reference system.

For example:

N4 = First Year of Primary Education

N9 = Final Year of Primary Education

N10 = First Year of Secondary Education

N15 = Final Year of Secondary Education

N16 = First Year of University

This means that educational credentials can be understood internationally without requiring another country to translate its entire grade system.

⸻

XIV. THE NAHOURI EDUCATION EQUATION

The system can be summarized conceptually as:

