XV. THE THREE-LANGUAGE CIVILIZATION

A Nahouri graduate should ideally be able to say:

English allows me to communicate with the world.

TlebiAfirikikan connects me to Africa and the African diaspora.

FuturLang allows me to communicate with future scientific and technological civilization.

My local language connects me to my community, history, and heritage.

This creates a model of education that is simultaneously:

Global + African + Technological + Multilingual + Culturally Pluralistic

