XVI. THE NAHOURI PRINCIPLE

The Nahouri Education System is ultimately founded on one principle:

“Standardize knowledge, not culture. Universalize opportunity, not identity. Teach the past, master the present, and mathematically prepare for the future.”

The complete Nahouri educational pathway is therefore:

N1–N3 → Foundation

N4–N9 → Primary

N10–N15 → Secondary

N16–N18 → University

with:

English + TlebiAfirikikan + FuturLang + Local Language

and with:

Mathematics + Science + Computing + Humanities + Creation + Mathematical Futurology

forming the intellectual foundation of a standardized global education system.
